1
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:06,860
Alchemy, the science of understanding,
deconstructing, and reconstructing matter.

2
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:09,980
However, it is not an all-powerful art.

3
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:12,920
It is impossible to create
something out of nothing.

4
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:17,420
If one wishes to obtain something,
something of equal value must be given.

5
00:00:17,480 --> 00:00:21,600
This is the law of equivalent exchange,
the basis of all alchemy.

6
00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:25,080
In accordance with this law,
there is a taboo among alchemists.

7
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:27,680
Human transmutation is strictly forbidden.

8
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:30,960
For what could equal the value
of a human soul?

9
00:00:31,380 --> 00:00:34,860
Kono omoi wo keshite shimau niwa

10
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:37,200
mada jinsei nagai dsho?

11
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:43,640
Yarinokoshite'ru koto
yarinaoshite mitai kara

12
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:59,640
Yume no tsuzuki oikakete ita hazu na no ni

13
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:05,980
Magarikunetta
hosoi michi hito ni tsumazuku

14
00:01:05,980 --> 00:01:12,900
Ano koro mitai ni tte modoritai wake ja nai ni
Nakushite kita sora wo sagashite'ru

15
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:14,520
Wakatte kuremasu you ni

16
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:19,680
Gisei ni natta you na
kanashii kao wa yamete yo

17
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:23,140
Tsumi no saigo wa namida ja nai yo
Zutto kurushiku seotte'ku n da

18
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:26,520
Deguchi mienai kanjou meiro ni
dare wo matte'ru no?

19
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:30,100
Shiroi nooto ni tsuzutta you ni
motto sunao ni hakidashitai yo

20
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:33,240
Nani kar nogaretai n da
genjitsu tte yatsu?

21
00:01:33,240 --> 00:01:39,940
Kanaeru tame ni ikite'ru n datte
Sakebitaku naru yo Kikoete imasu ka?

22
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:45,040
Bunai n nante yatte'rarenai kara

23
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:46,920
...kaeru basho mo nai no

24
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:50,220
Yasashisa niwa itsumo kansha shite'ru

25
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:53,700
Dakara tsuyoku naritai
(I'm on the way)

26
00:01:53,700 --> 00:01:57,360
Natsukashiku naru
konna itami mo kangei jan

27
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,000
Brother.

28
00:02:07,020 --> 00:02:07,740
Hmm?

29
00:02:07,780 --> 00:02:09,920
The stories about this priest in Liore...

30
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:11,280
You think they're true?

31
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:13,220
The ones about his "miracles"?

32
00:02:13,340 --> 00:02:16,180
They say he can transmute flowers
out of thin air, right?

33
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:18,980
Could just be slight of hand,
some cheap trick like that.

34
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:21,420
But...what if it's not?

35
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:22,520
Right.

36
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:26,040
If it's not, then I suppose all
that leaves is the real thing, huh?

37
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:31,000
The celestial stone that destroyed
the city of Xerxes in one night,

38
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:34,080
the grand elixir sealed
away by the Eastern Sage.

39
00:02:34,180 --> 00:02:37,240
It goes by different names,
but it's always the same thing,

40
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:39,880
some kind of object
that amplifies alchemy.

41
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,500
That's the Philosopher's Stone.

42
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:46,660
If we could just get our hands on it somehow,
I might be able to get your body back.

43
00:02:47,580 --> 00:02:51,760
Damn books!
They tell us everything but how to find it!

44
00:02:52,420 --> 00:02:53,120
Al?

45
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:53,980
Yeah?

46
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:56,440
I think I have a good
feeling about this one.

47
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:58,620
Mmm, me too.

48
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:03,480
Translation: Resembool, 10 years earlier
Ed? Al? Where are you?

49
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:05,700
Oh, you boys.

50
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:08,880
Are you in here messing
up your dad's study again?

51
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:12,160
And Ed, you know better
than to scribble on the floor.

52
00:03:12,220 --> 00:03:14,140
Yeah, but it's not scribbling.

53
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:15,320
Here, watch!

54
00:03:17,540 --> 00:03:18,460
Oh, my!

55
00:03:18,540 --> 00:03:20,240
That's alchemy, isn't it?

56
00:03:21,420 --> 00:03:23,100
Did your dad teach you that?

57
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:25,440
How can he teach us
anything if he's not here?

58
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:27,660
Right, we read about it in these books!

59
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:29,700
I can't believe you've done this.

60
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:33,180
I'm sorry, did we mess up?

61
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:35,200
No, no! It's great!

62
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:36,960
You definitely take after your father.

63
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:39,520
My little geniuses,
you make me so proud!

64
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:40,820
ED (Narrating): And that was it!

65
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:43,100
Mom had given us all the
encouragement we needed.

66
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:46,110
From that moment,
we were obsessed with learning alchemy.

67
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:49,940
But then, in the summer of that same year,

68
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:51,780
an epidemic swept the country.

69
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:54,100
The sickness came and it took her.

70
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:57,420
Hey, brother?

71
00:03:57,460 --> 00:03:59,140
I'm hungry, aren't you?

72
00:04:01,440 --> 00:04:02,840
And it's cold here.

73
00:04:02,860 --> 00:04:04,500
Let's go home, please.

74
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:07,940
Once dad comes back, everything'll be—

75
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:09,520
Don't even talk about him!

76
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:12,240
That bastard doesn't care about us.

77
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:15,640
He's not our dad.
He didn't even come for Mom's funeral.

78
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:26,600
You know, there might be
a way we could bring Mom back.

79
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:32,080
But I thought it said in all the books that using alchemy to
make people is something you're not supposed to do, ever.

80
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:32,900
That's right.

81
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:34,680
That's why it'll be our secret.

82
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:37,360
I thought I'd find you here.

83
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:39,240
What do you want, Winry?

84
00:04:39,260 --> 00:04:40,960
You know what my grandma says?

85
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:44,240
She says you shouldn't cry for
loved ones who've passed away.

86
00:04:44,380 --> 00:04:48,090
Because when you do, it makes
them feel sad in the next world, too.

87
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:50,090
We're not crying!

88
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:54,480
And who are you to talk anyway?

89
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:58,320
Every time your parents go away somewhere,
you cry like a little baby!

90
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:00,800
I... I do not!

91
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:02,680
Are you sure, baby?

92
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:04,960
I'm so stupid for worrying about you!

93
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,940
I'm going home to tell Grandma
not to make you any dinner!

94
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,980
ED: Hey! What are you gonna do that for?!

95
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,160
ED: Hold up!
AL: Yeah, wait for us!

96
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:14,340
Thanks for dinner!

97
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:19,480
Come on, Ed. Drink your milk, too.

98
00:05:19,980 --> 00:05:21,720
No, I hate milk.

99
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:24,080
If you don't drink it,
you'll stay short forever.

100
00:05:24,080 --> 00:05:25,840
You mean like you,
you sawed-off old hag?

101
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:27,840
What was that,
you little half-pint midget?!

102
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:30,180
- Shrunk down, mini-witch!
- Micro pee-wee!

103
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:32,600
- Baby ant baby!
-Subatomic shrimp!

104
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:35,480
[SCHOOL BELLS RINGING]

105
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:38,660
WINRY: You're reading those weird
books in the middle of class again.

106
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:40,620
You need to pay attention to the lessons!

107
00:05:40,780 --> 00:05:42,340
ED: Leave us alone, will ya?

108
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:44,140
WINRY: So, what kind of books are they anyway?

109
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:45,360
It's a secret.

110
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:47,780
In other words, it's none of
your damn business, Winry!

111
00:05:47,780 --> 00:05:50,380
C'mon, no fair!
You guys are always keeping secrets.

112
00:05:50,620 --> 00:05:51,500
[AL GIGGLES]

113
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:53,780
AL: Bye, Winry!

114
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:55,720
[GASP]

115
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:57,400
Hey!  I forgot!

116
00:05:57,420 --> 00:05:59,960
Grandma wanted me to tell you
she's making stew tonight!

117
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:01,200
Yay, stew!

118
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:03,200
Right, we'll be there.

119
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:07,480
ED: Y'know, whoever invented stew
must have been a genius.

120
00:06:07,580 --> 00:06:10,140
It's even got milk in it,
and it still tastes good.

121
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:11,620
So that makes it genius?

122
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:15,720
Someone came up with the idea to pour
milk into vegetable soup for the first time, right?

123
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:17,360
That's a leap of imagination!

124
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:19,720
The kind a scientist needs
to be able to make, too.

125
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:21,240
I don't know, I guess that's true.

126
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:21,960
Sure it is!

127
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:23,520
Just one leap, that's all it takes.

128
00:06:23,540 --> 00:06:26,180
And it's what we need to
figure out human transmutation.

129
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:33,000
ED: And so we began searching for the key that would unlock
the secrets of human transmutation and bring mom back to life.

130
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:38,260
We trained with an alchemy teacher,
to prepare our bodies as well as our minds.

131
00:06:39,380 --> 00:06:44,520
It took years of constant effort,
but we wanted to see mom smile again. 

132
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:48,440
We wanted to go back to our lives with her
the way they used to be.

133
00:06:48,740 --> 00:06:51,720
That's what drove us, day and night.

134
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:53,720
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

135
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:01,600
And we're ready.

136
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:03,070
[RAVEN CAWING]

137
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:10,820
Water 35 liters; carbon 20 kilograms;
ammonia, 4 liters; lime, 1.5 kilograms;

138
00:07:11,020 --> 00:07:19,060
phosphorus, 800 grams; salt, 250 grams;
saltpeter, 100 grams; sulfur, 80 grams;

139
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:25,080
fluorine, 7.5 grams; iron 5 grams; silicon, 3 grams.

140
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:29,460
Right, now the construction formula.

141
00:07:31,540 --> 00:07:34,720
And finally, we need some soul data.

142
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:40,680
- Okay, this is it, Al.
- Mmm.

143
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:55,340
Ed, something doesn't feel right.

144
00:07:55,340 --> 00:07:57,340
[AL SCREAMS]
ED: Al!

145
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:05,440
No!

146
00:08:08,100 --> 00:08:10,340
It can't be... a rebound?

147
00:08:10,340 --> 00:08:11,480
Brother!

148
00:08:11,660 --> 00:08:15,200
Ed! Help...! Ed...!

149
00:08:16,060 --> 00:08:18,920
- Brother!
- Al!

150
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:25,060
Al?

151
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:28,600
Wait. What was I doing?
I just...

152
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:30,180
Hello.

153
00:08:32,460 --> 00:08:33,360
Who are you?

154
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:36,020
Oh! I'm so glad you asked.

155
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:38,160
I am called by names.

156
00:08:38,180 --> 00:08:43,380
I am the world, I am the universe,
I am God, I am truth,

157
00:08:43,380 --> 00:08:47,840
I am all, I am one, and I am also...

158
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:49,040
You.

159
00:08:49,500 --> 00:08:50,180
[GASP]

160
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:59,140
You have dared to knock on the door.
Now the door is open.

161
00:09:00,820 --> 00:09:03,060
[ED SCREAMING]

162
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:06,700
Quiet, child.
This is what you wanted, isn't it?

163
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:09,400
[SCREAM]

164
00:09:09,460 --> 00:09:12,160
I will show you the truth!

165
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:14,540
[SCREAM]

166
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:27,320
It was like all of the information in the world
was being poured into my brain at once.

167
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:30,860
It's too much!
It's too much, make it stop!

168
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:36,280
What's happening to me?!

169
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:39,020
Stop it! Make it stop!

170
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:41,840
Make it stop!
[GASPS]

171
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:44,260
My head felt like it was about to burst.

172
00:09:44,340 --> 00:09:48,960
But for instant, it all became clear.
The truth of everything.

173
00:09:49,020 --> 00:09:52,880
Mom... mom please!

174
00:09:59,460 --> 00:10:01,140
How was it?

175
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:08,320
I see... My theory of human
transmutation wasn't wrong.

176
00:10:08,340 --> 00:10:10,580
It can be done. It's possible!

177
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:12,880
It's still just missing something!

178
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:17,480
All of the answers I need are right here.
The truth about human transmutation!

179
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:20,260
Please, you have to show it to me again!

180
00:10:20,340 --> 00:10:22,040
I can't do that.

181
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:25,620
I've already shown you
all I can for the toll you've paid.

182
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,280
Toll? What toll?

183
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:28,640
This...

184
00:10:28,740 --> 00:10:30,400
Surely you knew.

185
00:10:35,380 --> 00:10:39,540
It's the law of equivalent exchange.
Right, young alchemist?

186
00:10:40,010 --> 00:10:44,010
[SCREAMS]

187
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:50,360
Dammit. This can't be happening!

188
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:56,460
It can't be... This wasn't...
This wasn't supposed to... NO!

189
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:59,300
He's gone, what I have done?!

190
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:06,660
Somebody help me. Somebody...
Please, Mom... Mom, please.

191
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:07,680
[GASP]

192
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:14,220
[CHOKED, GASPING BREATHS]

193
00:11:21,900 --> 00:11:24,960
No... this... this is wrong.

194
00:11:25,020 --> 00:11:28,100
This isn't..
This isn't what we wanted!

195
00:11:28,460 --> 00:11:33,320
[CRYING] Al... Alphonse... Alphonse!

196
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:35,280
Alphonse!

197
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:39,480
This is all my fault...
Alphonse, no...!

198
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:44,420
No, dammit!
You won't take him too!

199
00:11:44,520 --> 00:11:47,160
Give him back! He's my brother...

200
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:52,560
Take my leg! Take my arm!
Take my heart! Anything, you can have it!

201
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:54,400
Just give him back!

202
00:11:54,540 --> 00:11:57,740
He's my little brother,
he's all I have left!

203
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:04,400
Fullmetal Alchemist.

204
00:12:06,330 --> 00:12:09,040
HUGHES: Roy! Hey, you're still in Central?

205
00:12:09,440 --> 00:12:12,700
For now anyway. They're shipping me back
to Eastern Command this afternoon.

206
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:14,480
Well, now aren't you the lucky one.

207
00:12:14,520 --> 00:12:17,480
Next time you come here, I expect you to
have made Brigadier General.

208
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:18,760
You got that? Heh, heh.

209
00:12:18,780 --> 00:12:21,700
Easy for you to say.
[HUGHES LAUGHS]

210
00:12:21,780 --> 00:12:24,980
Oh, by the way, if you're leaving,
I'll go ahead and give this to you.

211
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:26,240
What is it?

212
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:29,960
Something you might find interesting, the final report on Isaac McDougal.

213
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:33,120
I'm guessing it hasn't reached your office yet.

214
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:34,300
No.

215
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:38,900
Xingese alkahestry, what's that?

216
00:12:39,040 --> 00:12:43,720
Apparently, that's something they have
to be honest, no idea. You don't know it?

217
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:45,820
No, it's the first I've heard of it.

218
00:12:46,780 --> 00:12:49,560
So, how're the Elrics doing?
You keeping those boys out of trouble?

219
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:52,080
I'm their commanding officer,
not their father.

220
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:52,860
Hmm.

221
00:12:53,700 --> 00:12:55,560
Hey, tell me something, Roy,

222
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:58,100
why'd you decide to make Ed
a State Alchemist anyway?

223
00:12:58,540 --> 00:13:00,100
He's just a kid.

224
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:05,220
I mean, military life isn't easy, you know.
That boy's gonna have to go through hell someday.

225
00:13:05,680 --> 00:13:07,720
You and I have certainly seen our share.

226
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:15,220
ROY: Hell, huh?

227
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:20,060
Oh, they've seen hell.
Both of them. And plenty of it.

228
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:26,040
Translation: "4 years earlier"

229
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:31,980
Lieutenant Colonel,
they're not in back either...

230
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:33,540
What is this?

231
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:35,040
Where are they?

232
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:38,040
Where are they? Where are the
Elric Brothers? I want them found!

233
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:39,580
[DOG BARKING]

234
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:42,800
Oh, hush, Den,
don't bark at our guest.

235
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:43,900
Yes?

236
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:49,420
Hey, what is this?!
You have no reason to come barging in here!

237
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:57,100
We went to your house, we saw the floor.
What was that?

238
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:59,080
What did you do?

239
00:14:03,020 --> 00:14:06,300
We're sorry. We didn't mean it.

240
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:11,060
We're sorry. We're sorry. We're sorry.

241
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:12,540
[AL'S ARMOR TREMBLING]

242
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:14,000
Wait, are you...?

243
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:16,580
MUSTANG: This is a surprise to say the least.

244
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:20,960
I'd heard reports that there was a brilliant alchemist
living in this town, so I came to check them out.

245
00:14:21,120 --> 00:14:25,980
The last thing I expected to find was a boy skilled enough to attempt human transmutation.

246
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:29,680
Or advanced enough to bond a soul to a suit of armor.

247
00:14:30,380 --> 00:14:34,160
I'd say he's more than qualified
to become a State Alchemist.

248
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:37,520
Should he choose to accept the position,

249
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:41,020
he'll be required to serve the military
in times of national emergency.

250
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:46,120
In return, he'll receive privileges and access
to otherwise restricted research materials.

251
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:51,840
Given time, they may be able to find
a way to get their bodies back, or even more.

252
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:56,060
Right after he came stumbling to my door,
half dead and covered in blood,

253
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:59,560
I went over to their house to
see for myself what had happened.

254
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:02,500
What was there...

255
00:15:02,660 --> 00:15:05,220
Whatever that thing was,
it wasn't human!

256
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:08,840
Alchemy created that abomination,
it nearly killed them,

257
00:15:08,940 --> 00:15:11,400
And you want to throw those
boys headlong into it?

258
00:15:11,460 --> 00:15:14,640
Would you really have them go
through that kind of hell again?

259
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:17,020
WINRY: Some tea?

260
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:19,940
Yes, thanks.

261
00:15:26,180 --> 00:15:28,560
Say, uh... Lieutenant?

262
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:32,580
Just Riza, please. It's Riza Hawkeye.
Nice to meet you.

263
00:15:37,240 --> 00:15:41,380
Lieutenant Riza, have you
ever had to shoot anyone?

264
00:15:43,920 --> 00:15:45,140
Yes, I have.

265
00:15:46,420 --> 00:15:48,160
I hate what you soldiers do.

266
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:53,040
Soldiers like you are the reason my mom and dad left
during the war, and soldiers are the reason they're dead.

267
00:15:54,400 --> 00:15:55,520
And now you...

268
00:15:56,060 --> 00:15:58,600
Now you're here to take Ed and Al away, too.

269
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:01,780
If they go, that decision will be theirs,
and theirs alone.

270
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:06,940
Yes. It's entirely up to them now.

271
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:11,060
MUSTANG: I'm not forcing you.
I'm merely offering you the possibility.

272
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:13,580
Whether to move forward or stay still.

273
00:16:13,580 --> 00:16:18,880
Will you sit in that chair, wallowing in self-pity?
Or will you stand up and seize the chance the military can give you?

274
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:22,280
It's their choice.
They choose their own path.

275
00:16:22,420 --> 00:16:28,540
If you believe the possibility exists for getting your bodies back
you should seek it out, keep moving, whatever it takes.

276
00:16:28,620 --> 00:16:32,480
Even if the way ahead
lies through a river of mud.

277
00:16:38,460 --> 00:16:41,980
Miss Riza, why did you become a soldier?

278
00:16:43,380 --> 00:16:44,220
[SOFT CHUCKLE]

279
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:46,920
Because there's someone I have to protect.

280
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:51,760
We're leaving.

281
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:52,720
Yes, so.

282
00:16:56,500 --> 00:16:58,780
HAWKEYE: Well, I guess this is goodbye, young lady.

283
00:17:00,620 --> 00:17:01,900
It's Winry.

284
00:17:03,340 --> 00:17:05,540
Right. Bye, Winry.

285
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:09,400
I hope we meet again someday.

286
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:12,800
HAWKEYE: Will they be coming?

287
00:17:13,020 --> 00:17:14,320
MUSTANG: They'll come.

288
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:17,740
HAWKEYE: That boy...I've never
seen anyone look so defeated.

289
00:17:17,780 --> 00:17:19,000
That's what you saw?

290
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:23,040
No. There was fire in those eyes.

291
00:17:29,620 --> 00:17:31,460
PINAKO: You sure you won't regret this?

292
00:17:31,700 --> 00:17:33,910
ED: Hmm. My mind's made up.

293
00:17:35,340 --> 00:17:37,760
How long will the surgery
and rehabilitation take?

294
00:17:37,760 --> 00:17:40,100
I'd say about three years, more or less.

295
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:43,660
I'll do it in one.

296
00:17:43,660 --> 00:17:44,710
[BOTH GASP]

297
00:17:45,400 --> 00:17:47,740
You'll have yourself spitting blood,
you know that?

298
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:52,280
Al?
Just hang in there a little longer, okay?

299
00:17:52,300 --> 00:17:54,520
Then we're gonna get you
your body back, I promise.

300
00:17:54,560 --> 00:17:58,100
Right. And while we're at it,
we'll get yours back, too.

301
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:04,380
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

302
00:18:12,820 --> 00:18:14,880
Seems like you're in perfect shape!

303
00:18:14,900 --> 00:18:17,100
Yeah, now I just need to try some alchemy.

304
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:19,340
I guess it's been a while
since the last time I used it.

305
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:23,840
I know. Not since the night we
tried to bring mom back, right?

306
00:18:28,820 --> 00:18:29,800
Brother!

307
00:18:29,860 --> 00:18:31,760
Yeah, I'd say that's right on the money—

308
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:35,580
No, it's amazing!
You didn't even use a transmutation circle!

309
00:18:35,620 --> 00:18:38,160
You perform alchemy
the same way that teacher does!

310
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:39,740
You can do it, too, can't you?

311
00:18:39,800 --> 00:18:42,000
Me? No. No way!

312
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:45,940
So you didn't see it, did you?

313
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:47,420
See what?

314
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:49,740
Uh...never mind.

315
00:18:49,780 --> 00:18:50,580
[CRASH]

316
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:53,840
Hey, you! Don't mess up my auto mail!
You know how hard I worked on that?!

317
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:57,220
Hell, if it's half as you throw
a wrench I'd be surprised!

318
00:18:57,660 --> 00:18:58,640
[GROANS]

319
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:02,620
For real... you could try acting more
like a girl and less like a gearhead.

320
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:05,940
You think I'm a gearhead? That's fine, but you had better get used to it!

321
00:19:06,180 --> 00:19:10,820
'Cause as long as you're wearing my automail,
you're stuck with this gearhead, whether you like it or not!

322
00:19:11,380 --> 00:19:12,300
Huh?

323
00:19:15,580 --> 00:19:18,600
It's unusual for you to
observe the examination, sir.

324
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:22,500
That's true, but I hear we have
a twelve-year-old boy taking the test.

325
00:19:22,700 --> 00:19:25,260
Thought I would come out and see
what all the excitement was about.

326
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:29,540
Ah, would that be a steel prosthetic?

327
00:19:29,900 --> 00:19:31,980
Happened during the Eastern conflict.

328
00:19:32,260 --> 00:19:36,140
I see. So you had a rough
time of it in Ishval, hmm?

329
00:19:37,120 --> 00:19:38,560
Who's he?

330
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:42,100
You idiot! That's his excellency,
Führer King Bradley!

331
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:43,860
Hmm.

332
00:19:44,620 --> 00:19:47,560
Thank you.
You may proceed with the examination.

333
00:19:49,180 --> 00:19:51,880
Do you need something to
draw transmutation circles with?

334
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:53,620
No, that's okay. I got it.

335
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:03,300
He's not even using a transmutation circle!

336
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:16,000
My, that's quite something, isn't it?

337
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:19,870
Führer!

338
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:27,300
You know, there are some people who would see
this as a good way to assassinate a VIP.

339
00:20:27,340 --> 00:20:30,870
In the future, you might wanna rethink
the way you conduct these examinations.

340
00:20:34,560 --> 00:20:35,380
Hmm!

341
00:20:35,500 --> 00:20:39,080
That's good! You clearly
have nerves of steel, young man.

342
00:20:39,760 --> 00:20:43,240
But... I'd say you still have
much to learn about the world.

343
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:44,120
Hmm?

344
00:20:46,640 --> 00:20:47,580
Ah!

345
00:20:47,620 --> 00:20:50,640
[CHUCKLING] You put a quite a show,
my naive young alchemist.

346
00:20:50,700 --> 00:20:53,380
Good luck with the rest of your exams.

347
00:20:54,540 --> 00:20:56,860
When did he draw his sword?

348
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:04,400
AL: I wonder if Ed's doing
all right on his exam.

349
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:06,980
Say, Al?

350
00:21:07,020 --> 00:21:09,040
Yeah? What is it?

351
00:21:09,280 --> 00:21:14,320
If Ed does become a State Alchemist...
does that mean you'll be going away?

352
00:21:16,600 --> 00:21:17,700
Yeah.

353
00:21:19,940 --> 00:21:23,580
MUSTANG: This silver pocket watch will serve
as proof of your state certification.

354
00:21:23,980 --> 00:21:26,620
This envelope contains your certificate of appointments.
(Translation: "East City, Eastern Command Center")

355
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:27,720
Heh...

356
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:31,040
And it would seem our Fuhrer
is not without a certain sense of irony.

357
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:32,000
Why is that?

358
00:21:32,080 --> 00:21:33,980
Nothing. Congratulations.

359
00:21:34,140 --> 00:21:36,820
You've just officially
become a dog of the military.

360
00:21:37,260 --> 00:21:41,620
By order of Fuhrer King Bradley,
this document certifies that Edward Elric

361
00:21:41,620 --> 00:21:44,260
has been appointed to
the post of state alchemist,

362
00:21:44,260 --> 00:21:47,200
and that he is hereby
granted the title of Fullmetal.

363
00:21:49,660 --> 00:21:50,580
Fullmetal?

364
00:21:50,620 --> 00:21:51,460
That's right.

365
00:21:51,620 --> 00:21:54,800
Along with their commission,
State Alchemists also receive a codename.

366
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:57,660
Officially, you will now be known as...

367
00:21:57,660 --> 00:21:59,660
The Fullmetal Alchemist.

368
00:22:00,980 --> 00:22:03,940
I like that. It's nice and intimidating.

369
00:22:04,980 --> 00:22:07,420
I think that'll suit me just fine.

370
00:22:11,300 --> 00:22:14,780
AL: Hey, wake up...we're almost there!

371
00:22:18,540 --> 00:22:20,420
ED: So that's Liore?

372
00:22:21,680 --> 00:22:26,160
Could it really be there? The key to
finally getting Al his body back?

373
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:28,480
The Philosopher's Stone!

374
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:34,300
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

375
00:22:34,380 --> 00:22:39,600
nee kimi wa oboete imasu ka

376
00:22:39,660 --> 00:22:45,360
Yakusoku chigiri shoka
no kaze ga tsutsumu

377
00:22:45,620 --> 00:22:50,500
futari yorisotta

378
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:58,760
Muri na egao no ura

379
00:22:58,760 --> 00:23:04,140
nobita kage o kakumau

380
00:23:04,180 --> 00:23:13,520
Dakara kizukanu furi saisei o erabu

381
00:23:15,600 --> 00:23:22,740
Table no ue no furuenai shirase machitsuzukete

382
00:23:26,160 --> 00:23:31,580
kuuhaku no yoru o kuru hazu no nai asa mo

383
00:23:31,580 --> 00:23:35,880
zenbu wakatte'tan da

384
00:23:35,960 --> 00:23:41,440
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

385
00:23:41,440 --> 00:23:46,640
nee itsuka omoidasu deshou

386
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:52,080
Hatasenakatta yakusoku o idaite

387
00:23:52,320 --> 00:23:57,140
futari arukidasu

388
00:24:00,020 --> 00:24:06,220
Having arrived in Liore, Ed and Al encounter Father Cornello,
a priest who claims he can perform miracles.

389
00:24:06,540 --> 00:24:10,560
Blinded by false promises of eternal
life and resurrection for the dead,

390
00:24:10,620 --> 00:24:16,480
Cornello's followers fail to see the blood red stone
that gleams on his finger, or realise what it means.

391
00:24:17,020 --> 00:24:20,020
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

392
00:24:20,020 --> 00:24:23,080
Episode 3: City of Heresy

393
00:24:23,400 --> 00:24:27,580
What happiness can possibly be gained
by looking away from the truth?
